      "title": "Market Overreaction and Optionality",
      "description": "Bill Ackman argues that the stock market acts as a short-term voting machine influenced by speculation and fear, which creates buying opportunities when great companies experience temporary setbacks. By purchasing dominant businesses like Alphabet or Chipotle during public scares at low earnings multiples, investors secure high initial earnings yields and unpriced upside optionality."
    }
  ],
